# Where Askr's worker-mode upload parser differs from PHP's, by php-src test name.
#
# scripts/phpt-uploads.py fails on a test listed here that passes (the divergence is
# gone: remove the line), and on a test not listed here that fails (a new divergence).
# Each line: mode, test, why. An entry is removed only when the test passes, never by
# argument. Per-request mode has no entries: PHP parses the body there itself.
#
# Every request in worker mode is sent with CRLF line endings, as real clients send it;
# the php-src tests use bare LF, which PHP tolerates and Askr's parser (RFC 2046) does not.

worker rfc1867_anonymous_upload             a file part without a name is dropped; PHP lists it in $_FILES under a numeric key
worker rfc1867_malicious_input              a field name with text after "]" is handed over as written; PHP drops the upload
